<title>AUSTRALIA: Telstra says to sign IBM deal this week.</title>
<headline>Telstra says to sign IBM deal this week.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned telephone company Telstra Corp Ltd said on Monday it expects to finalise its three-way information technology joint venture with Lend Lease Corp Ltd and IBM on Wednesday.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not quite there yet, but we hope to sign on Wednesday,&quot; a Telstra spokesman said, but would not comment on what was still to be resolved.</p>
<p>Under the proposed alliance, Telstra will transfer about 2,500 information technology staff to the ISSC venture and have a 26 percent stake in the enlarged company, with Lend Lease and IBM stakes reduced to 23 percent and 25 percent respectively.  </p>
<p>The ISSC venture was first touted about two years ago.</p>
<p>-- Kevin Morrison 61-2 9373-1813</p>
</text>
